  "foaf:name": "An observatory of the North Atlantic Gateway",
  "sdo:name": "An observatory of the North Atlantic Gateway",
  "sdo:description": "Creating synergies between the Fram Strait LTER site &quot;Hausgarten&quot; and the Icelandic benthic inventory gained from BIOICE (Benthic Invertebrates of Icelandic Waters 1992-2004) and IceAGE  (Icelandic marine Animals: Genetics and Ecology since 2011) is the goal of this international 5-year project ALONGate (A long-term observatory of the North Atlantic  Gateway to the Arctic Ocean). The project focusses on deep-sea benthos, its  connectivity, and anthropocene impact on Vulnerable Marine Ecosystems (VMEs). The project and its intenational network se used as a “kickoff” to strengthen collaboration and promote the importance of the region, the “North Atlantic Gateway to the Arctic” on a higher international level.",
  "sdo:location": "Germany",
  "sdo:identifier": "48.8",
  "sdo:url": "https://oceandecade.org/actions/an-observatory-of-the-north-atlantic-gateway/",
